PANTHEON SEMANTIC SEED: LOOM-001

Coordinates: CHIMERA × LOOM × PARALLAX × DELTA OBSERVATORY × INDIGO HAMMER × ARGUS.

Question: What changes when six differently sensing agents exchange observations through different graph topologies, then one sensor modality abruptly becomes misleading?

World: Binary hidden truth; independent binary signals from 2 visual, 2 acoustic, 2 thermal agents; 240 steps; shift at 120; paired seeds.

Agents: Equal votes vs calibration fixed at shift vs online adaptive sensor reliability vs oracle ceiling. Truth becomes available only after each decision. One-hop communication networks: isolated, chain, hub, split, complete.

Result from 200 seeds, late postshift accuracy: isolated adaptive 77.8%; chain adaptive 84.3%; complete adaptive 94.2%. Complete fixed 44.0%, despite total consensus. This demonstrates consensus can amplify error when a shared inference mechanism goes stale in this toy world; not a general theorem.

Operators: local observe → network exchange → infer → act → reveal feedback → adapt → compare FPV / team / overhead → perturb → falsify → abstract → reconstruct.

Boundary: This is an executable binary-signal proof of concept, not the promised full sensory/physics/game engine. Topology and information-budget effects are confounded. No physical synthetic sense or human tool has been verified.

Next necessary tests: degree/bandwidth-matched rewiring; correlated/noisy/adversarial sensing; delayed labels; active perception; real continuous sensor encoders; human translation experiments.

